SUMMARY:QC and TAT Driving Change Project Event
LOCATION:333 S Franklin St Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Quality Carriers\, Inc. (QC) and TAT cordially invite you to s
 tand with us in the fight against human trafficking. Please join us for a 
 vital community initiative and public safety event showcasing TATs new\, s
 tate-of-the-art mobile exhibit designed to raise critical awareness across
  North America. What: Driving Change Project Mobile Exhibit and Awareness 
 Event When: Wednesday\, November 18\, 2026\, 9:00 AM - 3:00 PM ET Where: T
 ampa Convention Center\, Outdoor Parking Lot by the Riverwalk\, Tampa\, FL
  The Driving Change Project is a cutting-edge\, mobile walkthrough exhibit
  that serves as an educational museum. The exhibit features first-hand sur
 vivor stories\, impactful artifacts\, and educational resources. This inte
 ractive experience helps communities\, transportation professionals\, and 
 local leaders recognize the signs of human trafficking and learn how to ta
 ke effective action to combat this criminal enterprise. QC is proud to par
 tner with TAT to bring this exhibit to Tampa. This initiative represents o
 ur long-standing commitment to public safety\, supporting law enforcement\
 , and protecting the most vulnerable members of our communities. To help u
 s finalize planning and logistics\, please RSVP by filling out This Form .
  In the meantime\, you can learn more about our shared mission and find ad
 ditional education by visiting TATs Website . Additionally\, you can infor
 m others about this event by printing and hanging our Event Save the Date 
 Flyer . We look forward to seeing you on November 18 as we make a differen
 ce together. For additional questions or concerns\, please contact Bruce G
 acsal (Sr. Director - Security) at bgascalqualitycarriers.com . Sincerely\
 , QC and TAT \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa.gov/node/195586
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/195586
END:VEVENT
