 t to 22 All-State Ensembles featuring Floridas top Band\, Orchestra\, Chor
 us\, Guitar\, and Elementary students conducted by world-class conductors 
 and teachers. It is attended by more than 10\,000 people\, including secon
 dary music directors\, elementary music teachers\, music supervisors\, col
 lege students\, college music teachers\, school administrators\, K-12 stud
 ents performing in the All-State ensembles\, students and professional mus
 icians performing with invited performing ensembles\, exhibitors\, and par
 ents of performing students. Tickets for the All-State Performances will b
 e available at registration on a first come first serve basis. For more in
 formation\, please call (800) 301-3621 or visit www.flmusiced.org (http:ww
 w.flmusiced.org) For event details: www.fmea.org (http:www.fmea.org) or (8
 00) 301-3632 The FMEA Professional Development Conference is one of the la
